{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nClosing a large epic runs the completion-verifier close gate, whose final\n`decide@then/verify` step makes an LLM (Bedrock `converse`) call. On epic\n`3d7a-7795-efde-4df7` (REB-3233, 13 children) the gate ran ~40 minutes and then\nFAULTED — it produced **neither PASS nor FAIL/BLOCK**, but an error:\n\n```\ncannot close 3d7a-7795-efde-4df7: completion verification could not run\n(completion verification workflow did not produce a verdict:\n step 'decide@then/verify' failed: the LLM provider call failed:\n Read timeout on endpoint URL:\n \"https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/model/us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6/converse\").\n```\n\nThis is a fault in the gate itself: a transient/among-oversized provider Read\ntimeout is surfaced as \"could not run / no verdict\", so a legitimate close cannot\ncomplete without `--force`. Reproduced deterministically: three consecutive close\nattempts on this epic all faulted identically (~40+ min each, EXIT 1).\n\n`src/rebar/llm/failure.py:271` classifies `httpx.ReadTimeout`\n(`httpx.TimeoutException`) as `WAIT_AND_RETRY`, and `config.py` documents a retry\npolicy over transient timeouts — yet the gate still terminated with no verdict via\n`completion_failures.py:232` (\"... did not produce a verdict\"). So either the\nverifier's decide-step path does not apply the retry, retries are exhausted because\neach attempt sends an oversized accumulated context that itself read-times-out, or\nthe effective per-request timeout is too low for a large-AC epic-close verification.\n\nThis defect class has rich history (verifier sharding `12b7`, banked/resumable AC\nverification `2948`, context reworks `10ae`, step-budget loops `46a2`/`3211`,\n`REBAR_LLM_TIMEOUT` wiring `02cd`, Bedrock provider seam+timeout `061c`, gates\nrunning minutes-scale `1e88`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A transient provider Read timeout during the completion verifier's\n  `decide@then/verify` step no longer terminates the gate with \"could not run / no\n  verdict\"; it is handled per the WAIT_AND_RETRY classification (bounded retry) OR\n  the verification work is bounded so a single call cannot exceed the provider read\n  timeout — root cause to be confirmed by /rebar-debug before the fix. Proven by a\n  RED→GREEN test that exercises the confirmed mechanism.\n- [x] A large-epic close (many children / large AC set) completes through the gate\n  without a raw provider read-timeout fault, or degrades to an actionable verdict\n  rather than an un-actionable \"could not run\".\n\n## Testing\n\n- [x] A unit/integration test reproduces the faulting path (verifier decide step\n  raising `httpx.ReadTimeout`) and asserts the post-fix behavior (bounded retry\n  and/or bounded context / actionable outcome), seen RED before the fix and GREEN\n  after, with a mutation check."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787550510617784001,"uuid":"4f93197e-d93f-4f1e-b07e-e0f03fb5028e"}